# {{ENGINEERING_REPO}} — {{PROJECT_NAME}} engineering (code)

The **code** arm of {{PROJECT_NAME}} — the third context alongside `{{DS_REPO}}` (Figma design system) and
`{{STUDIO_REPO}}` (Figma screens + prototype). It turns the design system + validated screens into
shipping software. Platform: **{{PLATFORM}}**.

## What lives here
- **`{{COMPONENT_LIB}}` + Storybook** — the ONE coded implementation of {{SYSTEM_NAME}}, token-synced from
  the Figma DS, consumed by {{PROTO_CONSUMER}} AND the {{APP_KIND}}. *(component-engineer)*
- **The {{APP_KIND}}** — {{APP_STACK}}, {{APP_ID_LABEL}} `{{APP_ID}}`, composed from the shared library +
  the validated screens. *(app-engineer)*
- **The release** — the {{DEPLOY_UNIT}}, versioning, public declarations, and the ship to
  {{RELEASE_TARGET}} ({{RELEASE_PROJECT_LABEL}} `{{RELEASE_PROJECT}}`). *(build-uploader)*

## The one idea
**One coded library, three consumers** (Storybook · prototype · app). The thing you usability-test is the
thing you ship, so prototype→app rework is near-zero.

## Boot
Read `AGENTS-HANDOFF.md` for the roster, pipeline, cross-context seams, and the three gates this context
adds (parity · {{VERIFY_GATE}} · release). `CLAUDE.md` has the working notes. `DESIGN.md` is shared with
the other two contexts. Agents: `component-engineer`, `app-engineer`, `build-uploader`. Commands:
`/component-build`, `/app-build`, `/release`.

## Boundaries
Consumes the published Figma DS (`{{DS_REPO}}`) as coded tokens/components and the validated screens
(`{{STUDIO_REPO}}`) as the app's spec. A Figma DS gap routes to `{{DS_REPO}}`; a flow change to
`{{STUDIO_REPO}}`. Secrets (production credentials, signing material) stay gitignored.
